if you've managed to secure a ps5 during  its first year on the market there are  plenty of top-notch games you can enjoy  with your kids in today's video i'll  give you 10 of my favorite ps5 titles  that would make excellent gifts this  holiday season and don't worry i'll do a  quick recap of all 10 games at the end  and also include links to all of them in  the description below today's video  we'll start off the list with what is  undoubtedly my favorite ps5 game to play  with my son sack boy a big adventure  it's actually one of the best  platformers i have played in years not  even kidding here seriously guys we're  talking nintendo and mario level quality  here if you remember the old little big  planet games that formula goes almost  completely out the window with a big  adventure the latter is a 3d platformer  developed by sumo digital and not media  molecule the original creators of the  series the game is divided up into a  series of hub worlds and while it's  described as a 3d platformer there are a  number of different ways sumo switches  up to perspective throughout the game  with tweaks to level design along the  way it does operate from a fixed camera  perspective which kind of gives it the  feel of something like super mario 3d  world each level has a ton of  collectibles to find and challenges to  complete there are hundreds of different  costume pieces for your sackboy some of  which are found hidden throughout the  levels and others you can purchase with  gold you collect in-game sacboy manages  to strike that perfect balance of  presenting just enough of a challenge to  be difficult but not too frustrating for  inexperienced gamers to lose interest  although you can play sackboy solo the  game shines brightest when you play  alongside a friend or even a group of  friends a total of four players can team  up and while online play is supported my  son and i had an absolute blast playing  at his couch co-op seriously just so  many laughs i cannot recommend this game  enough up next we have ratchet and clank  rift apart which is a brand new entry in  the popular series from insomniac this  one is an absolute  graphical stunner on the ps5 hardware  and has received near unanimous praise  from fans and media alike if you've  played a ratchet game before you'll know  what to expect here if not imagine a  high-energy third-person shooting game  with off-the-wall weapons packaged  together in an experience that looks  like a pixar movie plus a fun story to  tie it all together where rift apart  iterates on the established formula is  by introducing rifts throughout the game  which open portals to other worlds  players can use these rifts to jump to  other locations in the game almost  instantly this sets the stage for unique  gameplay moments unlike what you've  experienced in the series before it's so  incredibly clear playing through this  game just how much insomniac has  mastered their craft over the years the  levels are just absolutely brilliant the  gameplay fun and engaging and did i  mention just how gorgeous it all is our  next title is a fresh take on a  platforming classic it's crash bandicoot  4 it's about time now if you're an old  school gamer like me you may be thinking  i'm incredibly cruel to recommend a  crash game for kids when you consider  just how tough the original games were  and don't get me wrong they were pretty  tough but you'll be happy to know crash  4 should please both new and retro  gamers by offering two difficulty  options modern which is more accessible  for new players and retro which will  appeal more to the hardcore fans of the  series regardless of which difficulty  you play on the game feels like classic  crash with a fresh coat of paint and  some new enhancements reviewers praised  the game for its quick and challenging  platforming beautiful environments and  strong replayability thanks to bonus  flashback levels local co-op competitive  multiplayer and plenty of unlockables  for something the whole family can enjoy  check out overcooked all you can eat  which is a compilation of both the  original overcooked and overcooked 2. if  you've never played an overcooked game  before it doesn't take long for things  to get just outright ridiculous the  setup is pretty straightforward prepare  food for customers in a given amount of  time but then you know the game's going  to throw plenty of obstacles along the  way that's going to make this a much  easier task said than a task done the  levels shift change and add new elements  as you try to progress which only result  in more insane moments this is one of  those titles where you'll probably want  to check your competitive ego at the  door and just enjoy the journey after  all i can't promise this one won't  result in some shouting and yelling as  you try and coordinate with your family  members to complete the orders  accurately and on time now our next  title is one that's completely free  that's right as long as you own a ps5  you can get this title totally free in  fact it's the very first game that i  recommend you boot up when you get your  ps5 it's astros playroom which is a game  that completely blew me away my son  who's a huge fan of mario games has also  enjoyed astro's playroom immensely it  was really his first introduction to  playstation to be honest i can't think  of a better way for a kid to learn about  playstation for the first time like i  mentioned i love this game so much it's  definitely the first one you should play  when you put up the system for the first  time it's a 3d platforming adventure  that will take you through the history  of playstation it also serves as an  incredible showcase for the new dual  sense controller and while astro is an  absolutely phenomenal showcase for the  controller the fact that it ends up  being so much more than that is what i  truly found surprising you'll move about  a series of different worlds that  represent generations of playstation  consoles astro will take on various  enemies and platform challenges along  the way you'll have a simple punch  attack spin attack and laser when astro  hovers to help you take care of the  enemies there are collectible puzzle  pieces and artifacts to find in each  world the puzzle pieces you find are  added to a giant puzzle in the game's  hub area whereas the artifacts are  pieces of playstation's history that  also make their way into that hub with  astros playroom it's all about the tiny  little details of nostalgia that really  helped to put it over the top there's so  many little nods and secrets that i just  don't want to even try and spoil them  all here it's far better if you  experience these for yourself the game  will only take you about four to six  hours to complete and really that's  honestly the only problem i had with it  after it was over i just wanted more  both my son and i were sad to see it end  but what a ride it was hopefully this is  only the beginning for astro on ps5  because i would honestly love to see a  sobe team get a shot at making a full  length 3d platformer featuring astro now  while astro is a celebration of all  things playstation one of the first pc  titles i ever played as a kid was sim  theme park unfortunately that series  isn't around anymore today but planet  coaster may be the next best thing like  sim theme park and roller coaster tycoon  before it planet coaster is a strategy  game where players set up and manage  theme parks there are four primary modes  in the game career sandbox challenge and  a scenario editor players become a theme  park manager in the career mode and are  tasked with completing various scenarios  to earn a bronze silver or gold star  which factor into your overall career  level then there's sandbox mode which  allows you to create your own theme park  by shaping the land building up your own  roller coasters and setting up  concession stands with this one you'll  also have unlimited funds and where  sandbox mode is all about the fun  challenge mode is harder and you'll only  start with a small amount of money this  one places much more of an emphasis on  the funds that you have coming in to  help sustain your park the scenario  editor allows players to create their  own scenarios which can then be played  in the career mode or uploaded online to  challenge other players you know one of  the wonderful things about video games  is just how many different types of  experiences you can enjoy and our next  game is completely different from  something like planet coaster it's  chicory a colorful tale which is an  absolutely  gorgeous and charming title you can  enjoy on the ps5 chicory is essentially  a giant coloring book that tells a  unique story from a top-down perspective  chicory is the lone wielder of a magic  brush that adds vibrancy and color to  what is otherwise a simple world of  black and white when chicory  unexpectedly abandons her post as the  wielder our main character who's a  janitor at the wielder's tower takes it  upon herself to pick up the brush and  restore color to the world the painting  mechanic throughout the game is deeper  than you'd expect and you'll gain access  to multiple tools along your adventure  many reviewers praised chicory for its  accessibility to players of any skill  level you can tweak not only the  difficulty of combat but also that of  the puzzles in addition to the gameplay  it tells a very touching sympathetic  story which i won't spoil here when it  comes to playing with family or friends  this is one that's beautiful to watch  and also supports co-op play where a  friend can paint alongside you if you  have a kid who's more of the laid back  artistic type then you certainly can't  go wrong with a title like chicory up  next we have temtem a title that's  unabashedly inspired by pokemon but just  so happens to be a solid game in its own  right temtim is a massively multiplayer  creature collection adventure players  will catch tempt him and battle other  tamers sound familiar yet you can also  customize your house join a friend's  adventure or explore the six islands of  the airborne archipelago there's a story  campaign where you'll travel across  those six islands while doing battle  against an evil clan look the  similarities to pokemon are certainly  there but where nintendo series has  resisted turning into an mmo temtem  fully embraces it in temtem players from  around the world can join you in real  time living the adventure alongside you  and battling to become a top tamer  there's also a co-op adventure mode  multiple customization options and  competitive play one of the best aspects  of temtem is how new content is  constantly being added to the game in  the form of new events new missions new  cosmetics and even new temtem for the  older kids out there they may be ready  to try a teen rated title like kana  bridge of spirits kana is a 2021  action-adventure title from ember lab  and it's another on our list with  absolutely gorgeous graphics and art  design kana is a young spirit guide  who's been tasked with helping spirits  find eternal rest you'll control the  heroine from a third-person perspective  and use your staff to battle enemies  using light heavy and charged attacks  kanan will also collect spirit  companions known as rot along the way  the rot will aid kana in a number of  different ways throughout the adventure  this one lands that teen rating as it  does tend to focus more on mature themes  like death grief and forgiveness if  you've been curious about the battle  royale craze but prefer something a  little more lighthearted than say  fortnite you and the family should check  out fall guys ultimate knockout my son  and i played a ton of this one when it  first released and it's good to see fall  guys is still going strong today up to  60 players will drop in each game to try  and make their way through a series of  zany challenges while controlling  bizarre jelly bean shaped characters  only so many will make it through each  round until one is crowned the victor at  the very end some of the levels are set  up like an obstacle course with clear  inspiration from classic platformers  like mario galaxy and even tv shows like  wipeout there are also team-based levels  where players are randomly assigned a  team and then must work together with  other jelly beans to best the other team  the losing team's players are all  eliminated developer mediatonic has  worked hard to keep the game fresh and  they've added new themed seasons which  often come with new levels game modes  and cosmetics look i also have a video  up for the best switch games for kids  which you can check out on the left side  of your screen right now and as always  thank you all so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon

